---
import Doc from '../../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import Pager from '../../../components/Pager.astro';
const slug = 'getting-started/install';
---
<Doc slug={slug} title="Install">
  <h1>Install</h1>
  <p class="lede">Install the latest cortex release on Linux or macOS.</p>

  <h2>Pre-built binary <span class="badge">recommended</span></h2>
  <p>
    Releases publish <code>amd64</code> and <code>arm64</code> archives for Linux and macOS.
    The asset names are stable, so GitHub's <code>releases/latest</code> URL always downloads
    the newest published version.
  </p>
  <pre><code>{`OS=$(uname -s | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')
ARCH=$(uname -m)
[ "$ARCH" = "x86_64" ] && ARCH=amd64
[ "$ARCH" = "aarch64" ] && ARCH=arm64
[ "$ARCH" = "arm64" ] || [ "$ARCH" = "amd64" ] || { echo "unsupported architecture: $ARCH"; exit 1; }

curl -fsSL "https://github.com/atakang7/cortex/releases/latest/download/cortex-${OS}-${ARCH}.tar.gz" \
  | sudo tar -xz -C /usr/local/bin cortex`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Build the latest source</h2>
  <p>Use this when you want the current <code>main</code> branch rather than the latest release:</p>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/atakang7/cortex.git
cd cortex
go build -o cortex ./cmd/cortex
sudo install -m 0755 cortex /usr/local/bin/cortex</code></pre>

  <h2>About <code>go install</code></h2>
  <p>
    Do not use <code>go install github.com/atakang7/cortex/cmd/cortex@latest</code> for Cortex 2.x.
    The repository's historical module path does not carry the <code>/v2</code> suffix required by
    Go's semantic import versioning, so <code>@latest</code> can resolve the old v1 line instead of
    the current Cortex release. Use the release binary above for a versioned install.
  </p>

  <h2>Verify</h2>
  <pre><code>cortex --version</code></pre>
  <p>The version should match the latest release shown on GitHub.</p>

  <div class="callout info">
    <span class="ico">ℹ️</span>
    <div class="callout-body">
      <strong>What's next?</strong> cortex needs a model before it can start. Continue to
      <a href="/cortex/docs/getting-started/quick-start/">Quick start</a> to configure one.
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="docs-pager"><Pager slug={slug} /></div>
</Doc>
